B.cXH=new A.p("layerPanel",B.U,"Opt-in on-map LAYERS control (mapstudio-0814): true, or { align: topStart|topEnd|bottomStart|bottomEnd (default topStart \u2014 the opposite corner from overlayAlign's default, so both may be used together), title, on: false to disable }. Renders a floating card (collapsed = a circular layers button) listing this node's sourceLayers with a visibility toggle each, plus a FILTER popup for any layer declaring `filterable`. It writes the SAME runtime overrides as the mapSetLayerVisible / mapSetFilter actions, so panel state survives rebuilds and agrees with applet-driven buttons. REQUIRES this node's `id` (overrides are keyed by it); an id-less or layer-less glmap renders no panel. A layer declaring selectedFeature is omitted (it draws only the selection); `panel: false` on a layer opts it out. Absent = no panel and NO layout change (no Stack wrapper).",B.f,null)
B.cHn=new A.p("pinMode",B.W,"Opt-in tap-to-drop multi-pin mode: tapping empty map background (not a marker) appends an ordered pin row {seq, lat, lon} to pinsTable. Existing marker-tap actions are unaffected \u2014 a pin drop only fires when the tap misses every marker. Default off.",B.f,null)
B.cUh=new A.p("pinsTable",B.at,"Bound table storing dropped pins as ordinary rows (seq/lat/lon) \u2014 persists, exports, clears via normal row ops. Required for pinMode and for the route overlay/legs list below.",B.f,null)
